module

public import ReasLib.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.RelativeProj.QuasiCompact
import StacksCheckRecall

/-!
# Lemma 71.11.7

In Situation 71.11.1, let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S`, and `𝒜` a
quasi-coherent commutative graded `𝒪_X`-algebra. The relative Proj projection is quasi-compact
if one of the following holds: `𝒜` is of finite type over `𝒜_0`; `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜_1`
over `𝒜_0` and `𝒜_1` is a finite-type `𝒜_0`-module; or there exists a finite-type
quasi-coherent `𝒜_0`-submodule `ℱ ⊆ 𝒜₊` such that `𝒜₊ / ℱ𝒜` is a locally nilpotent
sheaf of ideals of `𝒜 / ℱ𝒜`.

The projection is expressed by `IsEtaleLocallyProj`, which requires affine-étale scheme
Proj presentations compatible with their canonical structure morphisms. The shared theorem
uses a chartwise version of the third sufficient condition: the source's global finite
quasi-coherent submodule restricts to finite submodules on the affine étale charts, supplying
this chartwise hypothesis. Quasi-compactness is étale-local on the target.
-/

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.RelativeProj SheafOfModules.RingedSite

universe u

/- Lemma 71.11.7. The relative Proj projection of a quasicoherent commutative graded algebra
is quasi-compact under any of the three finiteness alternatives. -/
@[stacks 084F] #check (AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace.RelativeProj.quasiCompact_of_finiteness :
    ∀ {S : Scheme.{u}} {X : AlgebraicSpace S}
    (𝒜 : GradedAlgebraSheaf.{u + 1, u} (commStructureSheafLift X))
    [𝒜.IsCommutative] (hqc : 𝒜.IsQuasicoherent)
    {P : AlgebraicSpace S} (π : P ⟶ X)
    (hπ : IsEtaleLocallyProj 𝒜 π),
    QuasiCompactFiniteness 𝒜 → QuasiCompact π)
